# Strict next-intl & Auth Feature Architecture

You MUST STRICTLY follow this project architecture. DO NOT deviate under any circumstances. This is the sole base rule for i18n and auth features.

## 1. next-intl Directory & Config

- Global dictionaries MUST live in `src/messages/{en,ja}/`:
  - `common.json`, `navigation.json`, `validation.json`
- Feature / layout dictionaries MUST be colocated with the feature:
  - Auth flows: `src/features/auth/{flow}/messages/{en,ja}.json`
  - Layouts: `src/components/layouts/messages/{en,ja}.json`
- Config: `src/i18n/request.ts`
- Runtime load: `src/i18n/message-loader.ts` + `src/i18n/message-registry.ts`
- Type source of truth: `src/i18n/messages.ts` (EN imports only)
- DO NOT create translation JSON files in any other folder.
- New feature messages MUST be registered in BOTH `message-registry.ts` AND `messages.ts`.
- Locales are `en` and `ja` only.

## 2. Mandatory Coding Constraints (i18n)

- ALWAYS use `next-intl`:
  - Client: `useTranslations('namespace')`, `useMessages()` for Zod
  - Server: `getTranslations('namespace')`
- NEVER hardcode UI text strings in `.tsx` / `.jsx` files.
- ALWAYS use nested keys in JSON where appropriate.
- DO NOT introduce any other translation library (`react-i18next`, `i18next`, etc.).

## 3. Auth Feature Folder Architecture

For every auth flow `{flow}` (e.g. `login`, `signup`):

```
src/features/auth/{flow}/
  component/{flow}.component.tsx   # logic, form, default export {Flow}Component
  component/{flow}.view.tsx        # presentational UI + useTranslations
  schema/{flow}.schema.ts          # create{Flow}Schema(messages) + Zod types
  type/{flow}.type.ts              # {flow}DefaultValues
  messages/en.json
  messages/ja.json
```

- NO barrel `index.ts` under auth features.
- App pages under `src/app/[locale]/(auth)/` MUST import only the component:
  `@/features/auth/{flow}/component/{flow}.component`
- View is imported ONLY by its sibling component (relative `./{flow}.view`).
- Message JSON shape:

```json
{
  "Auth": {
    "{flow}": { },
    "{flow}Validation": { }
  }
}
```

- UI copy: `useTranslations("Auth.{flow}")`
- Validation: `create{Flow}Schema(messages)` reading `messages.Auth.{flow}Validation.*`
- Types: `T{Flow}Schema`, `T{Flow}SchemaInput`, `T{Flow}SchemaOutput`
- Shared `Auth` root: when multiple auth flow JSONs are registered, deep-merge so `Auth.login`, `Auth.signup`, etc. coexist (shallow merge would overwrite).

## 4. Standard Workflow — New Auth Flow (e.g. signup)

1. Scaffold the folders/files under `src/features/auth/{flow}/` per section 3.
2. Add `en.json` + `ja.json` with `Auth.{flow}` and `Auth.{flow}Validation`.
3. Register loaders in `src/i18n/message-registry.ts` and EN import/deep-merge in `src/i18n/messages.ts`.
4. Wire the app page to import `{Flow}Component`.
5. Replace all UI strings with `t('key')`; preserve structure/styles; never hardcode text.

## 5. Standard Workflow — UI Text / Conversion

1. Extract all text into key-value pairs.
2. Append keys to ALL locale files (`en.json` and `ja.json`) in the correct dictionary path.
3. Replace hardcoded text with `t('key')`.
4. If the dictionary is new or moved, update BOTH `message-registry.ts` and `messages.ts`.

## 6. Strict Enforcement & Refusal

- REFUSE placing JSON dictionaries outside the paths in section 1.
- REFUSE auth UI outside `src/features/auth/{flow}/` or skipping the component/view/schema/type/messages split.
- REFUSE registering messages in only one of `message-registry.ts` or `messages.ts`.
- Stick strictly to `next-intl`.
